      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huachuca_City%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town grew after Fort Huachuca reopened in 1954, passing through names Campstone Station, Sunset City, Huachuca Vista before settling on Huachuca City.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huachuca_City%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fort Huachuca, just south of the town, once housed African American Buffalo Soldiers sent to the Southwest after the Civil War.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.thecrazytourist.com/15-best-things-to-do-in-huachuca-city-az/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Huachuca City sits in southwestern Cochise County, bordered by Sierra Vista and Fort Huachuca to the south.",
